From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucaszhongsj <lucaszhongsj@foxmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 10:41:10 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(acnh): the taller picture narrows to stay under the
 layout tables' 2048 rows

The game's layout tables stop at a display height of 2048 (0.9375 starts,
0.935 does not), and a taller display finds no layout entry for its capture
object: the rebuild path then reads the object it has cleared
(main+0x38497e0). A phone's upper half (0.92) asks for 2088, so the output
narrows instead of growing: 1880x2040 keeps the shape to 0.17%.

The size stubs now scale the game's own 1920-wide values by the output's
width as well as its height (state +0x64), the resolution table's entry and
the layouts' DrawInfo included. Two fixes of the game's own code come with
the taller picture: the fixed heap grows by 32 MB, because the display's
capture buffers and layers outgrow it (an allocation at main+0x37c6a10
fails), and the capture manager no longer takes its destroy path, which
leaves the null its frame reads.

Verified headless on a Mac at 3.0.3 main: 0.92 ran 1500 frames at 30 fps
with a screenshot of the scene, and 16:9, 1.43 and 2.17 still run.

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: the patch before it stopped at the 1536 display height it found; the
limit is the game's layout tables at 2048, and past it the capture manager
reads the object it clears, not only the actor manager its lookup. The output
narrows to stay under the limit, so a standing phone's upper half (0.92)
starts at 1880x2040, with the heap and the capture manager's destroy path
fixed for the taller picture.
Issue: none yet: no upstream issue for the picture shape

